  "content": {
    "id": "p64-q18-content",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "Fiona is playing a game. She throws $8$ balls at a target, one at a time. Each hit is worth $5$ points. Each miss is worth $-3$ points. Fiona hits the target with $5$ of the balls and misses with the rest.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p64-q18-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "How many points does Fiona score?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$16$ points.",
          "worked": "Number of misses: $8-5=3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}5\\times5+3\\times(-3)&=25+(-9)\\\\5\\times5+3\\times(-3)&=25-9\\\\5\\times5+3\\times(-3)&=16\\end{align*}$$\n\nFiona scores $16$ points.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p64-q18-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p64-q18-b-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Chris throws ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "9",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " balls at the target, one at a time.",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "break"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Is it possible for Chris to score the same number of points as Fiona?",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No. With $5$ hits and $4$ misses Chris scores $13$ points; with $6$ hits and $3$ misses he scores $21$ points. Each extra hit increases the score by $8$ points, so $16$ is impossible.",
          "worked": "With $5$ hits and $4$ misses:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}5\\times5+4\\times(-3)&=25-12\\\\5\\times5+4\\times(-3)&=13\\end{align*}$$\n\nWith $6$ hits and $3$ misses:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}6\\times5+3\\times(-3)&=30-9\\\\6\\times5+3\\times(-3)&=21\\end{align*}$$\n\nReplacing a miss with a hit increases the score by $5-(-3)=8$ points. Fewer than $5$ hits give a score below $13$; more than $6$ hits give a score above $21$. Since $13<16<21$, Chris cannot score $16$ points.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
